  steps:
    1. Start with an 18x18 all-grey grid.
    2. Place 3-5 qualifying components. For each, first place a solid black
       rectangle (2x2 to 4x2 or 2x3), then grow 2-6 thin black arms (width-1
       paths, no 2x2 blocks) from its edges. Total component size 6-17.
       Record rectangle positions for the output.
    3. Fill remaining grid area with random black noise at ~35-45% density,
       but ensure no new 2x2 all-black block is created. Use rejection per cell
       or iterative placement checking the 2x2 neighborhood constraint.
    4. The noise creates many small non-qualifying components (size 1-5) plus
       occasional larger thin components, matching observed distributions.
    5. Output = input with qualifying rectangles recolored red.
